WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.209
"Naturally Boosting AMPK
with Caloric Restriction for Life Extension"

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.920
In my book on everything
evidence-based in weight loss,

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.760
How Not to Diet, I had a section
entitled "Amping AMPK."

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.760
AMPK is an enzyme that acts
as a universal fuel gauge

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.800
for plants and animals,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.120
revving up
when it detects a depletion

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.440
of the universal fuel.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.320
The universal energy currency
in all of biology

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.120
is a molecule called
adenosine triphosphate,

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.480
commonly known as ATP.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.160
The tri in triphosphate means
three, as in tricycle or,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.120
in this case,
ATP's three phosphates

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.320
where energy is stored.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.960
Plants make ATP
with energy from the sun,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.760
and animals make it
by burning fat,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.760
carbohydrates, and protein.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.040
The energy is spent
by releasing the phosphates,

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.760
which transforms ATP to AMP,
adenosine monophosphate,

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.520
with mono meaning one,

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.720
which then can be juiced up
with two more phosphates

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.840
back to ATP,
and the cycle continues.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.160
In this way,
every cell in our bodies

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.480
and in every living thing

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.880
is like a little
rechargeable battery.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.600
AMP molecules are charged up
with phosphates to ATP

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.040
using sunlight or food

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.080
and then drained back down
to AMP

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.000
to do the cell's work.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.280
This brings us to AMPK,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.480
or AMP-activated protein kinase.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.240
A kinase is a type of enzyme.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.840
What might be the function
of an enzyme activated by AMP?

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.600
A buildup of AMP
means the rechargeable battery

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.960
is running low.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.360
It's akin to the fuel gauge
in your car reading empty.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.040
As the needle creeps toward
the E, what do you do?

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.720
Add more fuel.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.680
But instead of having
an extra gas can in your trunk,

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.640
you may have junk
in the trunk,

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.080
fat stores on your body.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.120
So that's what AMPK does:

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.640
It flips the switch
in your body

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.560
from storing fat
to burning fat.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.360
That's why AMPK
is not only known

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.120
as the "master energy sensor"
in our body

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.400
but the "fat controller."

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.360
No wonder I featured it
in How Not to Diet.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.440
But it can also control aging,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.080
and so also plays
a starring role

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.800
in How Not to Age.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.280
To sustain life,

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.800
each of our cell "batteries"
needs to stay fully charged.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.840
This means maintaining a ratio
of about 100 ATP for every AMP.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.160
So, our body needs
to perfectly balance

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.800
cellular activities
that consume energy

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.760
with cellular processes
that generate energy.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.200
In times of plenty,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.840
our cells can plow
full steam ahead.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.360
However, in lean times,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.520
which for animals
means not enough food,

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.920
and for plants
means not enough light

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.360
(darkness is like starvation
for plants),

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.960
AMPK kicks in
to reorient the cell

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.120
into conservation mode

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.040
and start tapping
into our energy stores,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.880
like burning off body fat.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.920
Our cells can also institute
a recycling program

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.320
called autophagy.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.200
Autophagy comes from the Greek
words auto, meaning "self,"

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.280
and phagein meaning "to eat."

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.720
So, autophagy literally means
"self-eating."

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.800
It's a housekeeping process

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.880
by which defective
cellular components

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.800
like misfolded proteins
that had been allowed

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.280
to wastefully build up
in times of surplus

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.080
are broken down and scrapped
for spare parts.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.680
This doubles as both salvage
operation and quality control,

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.000
scavenging raw materials
in scarce supply,

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.240
as well as clearing away
some of the buildup

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.480
of damaged debris
that is implicated

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.560
in the aging process.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.040
As one review put it,

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.920
"The janitor
is the undercover boss."

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.000
This is one of the reasons

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.680
AMPK is increasingly recognized
as a pro-longevity factor.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:47.000
AMPK induces autophagy,
which cleans house,

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.680
sweeps away accumulated waste,

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:53.280
and effectively institutes
a sort of cellular "reset."

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.160
There are three main ways

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:58.880
longevity researchers
establish an aging pathway:

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.240
Does the factor worsen with age?

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.120
If you amplify it,
does it accelerate aging?

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.680
And if you dampen it,
does it slow aging,

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.800
and thereby extend lifespan?

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.200
The loss of AMPK activity
as we age

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.960
fits all three criteria.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.000
Our levels of AMPK drop
as we grow older,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.120
and it gets harder to activate.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.280
When this decline
is exacerbated,

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.320
aging is hastened (at least
in the hearts of mice).

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.200
And when this process
is reversed,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.720
when AMPK activation
is boosted,

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.960
lifespan is extended
in model organisms,

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.600
as much as 38 percent

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.000
in a type
of microscopic roundworm

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.720
known as C. elegans.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.080
Up and down
the evolutionary tree of life,

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.960
one of the most reliable ways
to extend lifespan

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.560
may be long-term
food restriction.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.880
And AMPK activation is thought
to be one of the mechanisms

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.360
for this longevity boost.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.920
What was remarkable about
the AMPK boosting experiments,

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.720
though, is that animal lives
can be extended

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:03.400
even though they were allowed
to eat as much as they want.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.040
So, AMPK activators
can effectively fool the body

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.160
into thinking it is starving,

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.240
flipping it into
protective housecleaning mode

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.920
without having to suffer
the pangs of deprivation.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:18.640
AMPK activators
can thereby be considered

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.680
calorie restriction mimetics,
or imitators.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.600
No wonder AMPK is considered
a "druggable" target

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.480
for longevity.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:32.080
But is there a way we can
naturally boost AMPK activation

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.560
to slow aging
without starving ourselves?

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:56.640
The answer is yes,
which we'll explore next.

